{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 136, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a pooling shortcut for an identity shortcut keeps the residual path without pooling's blurring."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest operation on the input-to-output edge with identity loses representational capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a learnable convolution with a parameter-free identity removes capacity on the direct path."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Average pooling on the final edge into the output hurts, so replacing it with a 3x3 conv helps more than replacing none."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 2 already receives a convolutional signal from the input, a conv path from node 2 to the output adds more value."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing edge 0 cuts off node 1, which costs less when node 1 feeds only one downstream edge."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Identity is generally a better shortcut than pooling on edges into the output node."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "This removes a 3x3 conv from the node 1 to output path and loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "This adds an entirely new conv path into node